{
  "case": "due2-list-part-and-class",
  "source": "due2-native: hasPart and isA with a set right operand, written as an RDF list and as repeated values (decisions/0005, decisions/0013)",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. Closes the gap of #32: no case exercised hasPart or isA with a list, or a partOf closure longer than reflexivity under either. ex:exportListed and ex:exportRepeated state one hasPart constraint, ex:auditListed and ex:auditRepeated one isA constraint, each as odrl:rightOperand ( ... ) and as repeated values; both forms are one right operand, the set of the values (due2-profiles.md §4, decisions/0013), so each scenario of one form has a twin with the same answer. hasPart holds when every right value is part of some left value under the typed partOf closure, and isA when the left value is an instance of every listed class (decisions/0005). ex:SalesQ1 reaches ex:SalesData in two hops through the asset collection ex:SalesFY26. The class hierarchy is in the policy file; a role's rdf:type edge is world data, so it is in sotw.closure. W1 warns ContestedOperatorReading on all four constraints, in either form: on hasPart for its set-valued left operand and its set right operand, on isA for its set right operand. The case format records no warnings; tools/check_corpus.py emits them.",
  "prefixes": {
    "ex": "https://example.org/",
    "role": "https://example.org/role#",
    "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "list: hasPart, the package holds both parts",
